From: Guilhem Moulin <guilhem@debian.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Mar 2026 17:34:30 +0100
Subject: Avoid dependency on new package mlocati/ip-lib

mlocati/ip-lib is not present in Debian. The dependency was introduced
upstream in order to fix CVE-2026-35540.

Rebased for 1.7.4: upstream has since refactored is_local_url() to
delegate range checks to a shared is_ip_in_range() helper (also used for
proxy_whitelist checks against $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR']), so the
IPLib\Factory calls are removed from that helper instead of inlined in
is_local_url(). is_ip_in_range() now does its own CIDR matching against
inet_pton()'s binary representation. The obfuscated-IP-literal parsing
(inet_pton2(), for hosts like "0x7f.1" that inet_pton() rejects but
browsers still resolve) is unchanged from upstream's fix.

Restores (rebased onto tests/Framework/UtilsTest.php's current
PSR-4/attribute-based structure) the CVE-regression cases Debian's
original patch added to the test suite, plus one fix found while
restoring them: upstream's own $nets list in is_local_url() only
special-cases IPv4-*mapped* IPv6 addresses (::ffff:a.b.c.d,
'::ffff:0:0/96' below), not the older IPv4-*compatible* form
(::a.b.c.d, deprecated by RFC4291 2.5.5.1 but still resolved by
inet_pton(3) and so by PHP/curl) that Debian's original, inlined
version of this check also covered. Without it, a URL like
"https://[::127.0.0.1]" is not recognised as local - the same class of
obfuscated-IP-literal SSRF-filter bypass this CVE fix otherwise closes.
Added a parallel '::0.0.0.0/96' entry to close it back up.

Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1131182
Forwarded: not-needed
